WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.488
Unit 2 is the database axis.

2
00:00:02.488 --> 00:00:06.728
The data platform book's chapter on
the four-class pattern for applications

3
00:00:06.728 --> 00:00:10.609
describes two independent axes: how
users sign in to the application,

4
00:00:10.609 --> 00:00:13.401
and how the application
connects to the database.

5
00:00:13.401 --> 00:00:18.100
On the database axis, evidence places
each application in one of four columns.

6
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.025
A is configuration only.

7
00:00:20.025 --> 00:00:21.650
B is a code change.

8
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:23.275
C is vendor-dependent.

9
00:00:23.275 --> 00:00:25.237
And D is no Entra path today.

10
00:00:25.237 --> 00:00:29.520
The kit's scan reads each
application's configuration files,

11
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.059
masks every stored password, and sets
A, B, C or done, from the driver,

12
00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:38.513
its version, the host, and whether
a vendor owns the application.

13
00:00:38.513 --> 00:00:43.476
A string with no owner's file, or a driver
the table doesn't know, goes to review.

14
00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.425
The scan never sets column D.

15
00:00:45.425 --> 00:00:49.702
Only the owner can say a vendor has no
release coming or an application is

16
00:00:49.702 --> 00:00:54.050
to be retired, and that answer goes into
the exception registry, with a date.
